      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I also raised this issue before. It got so bad for me that i would rather stay in private worlds with friends. When I would go see friends in public worlds crashing almost seemed a routine thing I had to deal with. It was so frequent I used a wholesome mod client to protect myself with a spoofer that masks your IP. It worked very well. The mod client I used to use is outdated now and now migrated to a new mod loader but right now its not that bad in regards to crashers. I do have a fear of using mod clients now because during the last ban wave, I got hit with one of the bans even though I used the mod client responsibly. It took me four months of waiting to return to the game. It was also during the time the US entered quarentine which was the worst. I wish there was a method which allowed to use mods legally in the game or at the least a method in which to confirm toxic and malicious mod client players and ban them. Either that or go after malicious client developers and their discords and shut them down or at the least stop the use of their malicious tools.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
