  "details": "Just too bring this too light, 3 years later This is still an issue. I know Its an old topic. but I think its good that we keep an eye on this\nIts annoying when you are just hanging with friends in a public and get crashed / BSOD \"memory overflow / ran out of memory\" (when I have 32Gb of DDR4 Memory)\nBecause someone entered the world with a Global crash client or just I or my friends get kicked from the instance. \nIt is a hit or miss with public worlds so It is difficult too meet new people when these kinds of people affect public \nVER #1 Client user: \"I don't like you because your staring at a mirror\"\nVER #2 Client user \"I don't like different opinions \"\nVER #3 Client user \"omg Streamer hahahaa (crash) \nand spam racial slurs\" \nFirstly I want too make it clear. welcome too the internet people think different.\nHowever I do believe there needs too be a crack down on clients that are \"toxic\" such as but not limited to \nClients that use Bots too kick\nanti-block\nDDOS tools\nGlobal crash tools\nETC...\nHowever there are people out there that are \"wholesome\" client users and I understand that (This however could result in a blanket change which is not what I want too happen)\nsuch as but not limited to\nPLAY SPACE MOVER\nWORLD REJOIN\nANTI PORTAL (too stop pesky portal spammers AKA, people who use clients too spawn portals that have crash worlds)\nAnyhow, you get the idea, being a long time VRCHAT player I see this as being an issue and as a deterrent too new players and people who want to socialize \nOn the other hand, I see VRCHAT moving in a circular direction right now, new people come in and never come back. \nsome people stay and suffer through it. but I do see this getting better if it is brought up again too clarify it is still and is an issue\nPeople like me that are DISABLED and out of the ARMY / MILITARY (this is context of why I have so much time on my hands) have all the time in the world too be on this game \nhence why I am bringing this up.\nlet me know what you guys and gals think down in the comments",
